WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:03.560
Sausage Party leapt a ton of hurdles just
to get released.

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:08.630
Who knew a cartoon about a hotdog with a foul
mouth and some bun lust would spark so much

00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:09.740
controversy?

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:14.260
But for all the reactions to the film, the
weirdest stories happened behind the scenes.

00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:18.930
Here are some details about Sausage Party
that even hardcore fans may not know.

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:20.330
Child friendly

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:25.760
Sausage Party came about a dill slice away
from being burdened with an NC-17 rating in

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:30.680
the U.S., but the ratings board is apparently
a bit more relaxed in Sweden.

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:32.340
Because they let the movie with this...

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:37.320
"But once we're out the doors it's not a sin."

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:40.460
"For us to let you slip it in."

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:42.060
...and this…

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:45.980
"They're eating children!

00:00:45.989 --> 00:00:47.579
f------ children!"

00:00:47.579 --> 00:00:53.920
...hit theaters with an "11" rating, meaning
that kids aged 7 to 11 could go see Sausage

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:58.239
Party with an adult, and kids older than 11
could see it anytime they wanted.

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:00.780
Those parents must have been thrilled.

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:02.440
"Jesus C-----!

00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:07.549
She's peeling me f------ skin!"

00:01:07.549 --> 00:01:08.729
Happier ending

00:01:08.729 --> 00:01:13.630
The giant food orgy at the end of Sausage
Party came out of nowhere, but it was originally

00:01:13.630 --> 00:01:16.060
even more filthy than the final cut.

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:20.409
Writers Seth Rogen and Evan Goldberg gave
the animators free reign to be as creatively

00:01:20.409 --> 00:01:25.820
nasty as possible, and the result was 12 straight
minutes of food-on-food action.

00:01:25.820 --> 00:01:31.130
Rogen told IndieWire, "We found out that animators
can be pretty sick when told they can do whatever

00:01:31.130 --> 00:01:32.359
they want."

00:01:32.359 --> 00:01:33.729
The Naughty Dog

00:01:33.729 --> 00:01:39.439
Movie studios love a tie-in deal, but, as
Seth Rogen put it, "Shockingly, no major sausage

00:01:39.439 --> 00:01:43.859
company wanted to partner with a movie that
condemns the eating of sausages."

00:01:43.859 --> 00:01:48.439
However, the movie did manage to work out
a promotional tie-in with the hot dog restaurant

00:01:48.439 --> 00:01:49.560
chain Dog Haus.

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:54.509
"In conjunction with the Sony Pictures release
of Sausage Party Dog Haus is proud to present

00:01:54.509 --> 00:01:56.030
'The Naughty Dog.'"

00:01:56.030 --> 00:02:00.979
The Naughty Dog consisted of a spicy kielbasa
topped with onions and horseradish mayonnaise

00:02:00.979 --> 00:02:05.710
on a grilled bun, which sounds delicious,
but remember: that hot dog only wants you

00:02:05.710 --> 00:02:07.640
to love it.

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:12.860
"Frank!

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:14.140
Move your F------ A--!"

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:16.360
Casting call

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:21.069
One of the first people Rogen cast for Sausage
Party was his good friend, Oscar-nominated

00:02:21.069 --> 00:02:22.650
actor Edward Norton.

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:26.269
You know him mostly from roles where he doesn't
play an animated bagel.

00:02:26.269 --> 00:02:29.180
"I am Jack's smirking revenge."

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:37.200
Norton loved the concept for the Sausage Party,
and even came up with the idea for the character

00:02:37.209 --> 00:02:41.769
he'd eventually play, Sammy Bagel, Jr.—"a
bagel that sounded like Woody Allen."

00:02:41.769 --> 00:02:47.350
"The only thing I've ever pushed is my peaceful
agenda which that I didn't even push I ah

00:02:47.350 --> 00:02:49.019
passively aggressively nudged."

00:02:49.019 --> 00:02:53.620
Rogen also thinks that Norton's early involvement
helped assemble the all-star cast.

00:02:53.620 --> 00:02:57.090
"I think he was ultimately the one who talked
Kristen Wiig into doing it, also.

00:02:57.090 --> 00:03:01.030
He really helped wrangle the cast, and because
he was one of the first people involved in

00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:05.190
it, it was easy to get other people because
we always could say, 'We got Edward Norton

00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:06.190
in the movie!'"

00:03:06.190 --> 00:03:08.329
A different direction

00:03:08.329 --> 00:03:13.080
Animated movies are time-consuming to make,
so a lot of them have two credited directors

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:14.250
to split the workload.

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:19.250
This was also true for Sausage Party, which
was helmed by Conrad Vernon and Greg Tiernan.

00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:23.360
Content-wise, Sausage Party was a huge shift
for Tiernan in particular.

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:27.579
Although he's a veteran animator who worked
on projects like All Dogs Go to Heaven, Cool

00:03:27.579 --> 00:03:32.370
World, and The Tigger Movie, Tiernan's only
previous animation directing experience was

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:37.830
overseeing episodes of Thomas &amp; Friends, the
animated preschool series about trains with

00:03:37.830 --> 00:03:38.830
faces.

00:03:38.830 --> 00:03:42.620
"It's not your fault the weather stopped you
doing your job.

00:03:42.620 --> 00:03:46.900
And isn't the important thing that all the
children's letters get to Santa on time?"

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:49.670
And then...he did this:

00:03:49.670 --> 00:03:55.920
"Oh 'shroom...are you hit?"

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:56.939
Animator approved

00:03:56.939 --> 00:04:00.599
Sausage Party is messed up in most ways you
can imagine.

00:04:00.599 --> 00:04:01.790
Nobody's going to argue about that.

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:02.790
"I was afraid you left me because I wasn't
fresh anymore.

00:04:02.790 --> 00:04:06.030
And then I was attacked by a douche."

00:04:06.030 --> 00:04:08.840
But people in the animation industry seem
to love it.

00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:13.530
After Sausage Party hit it big at the box
office, Sony mounted an Oscar campaign for

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:17.570
the movie and held a special screening to
drum up Academy interest in the movie.

00:04:17.570 --> 00:04:22.260
Seth Rogen gave a speech at the event, and
afterward, Oscar-nominated animator Bill Plympton

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:26.880
came up to him and said, "When you gave that
speech before and everyone applauded, that

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:27.980
was just great.

00:04:27.980 --> 00:04:31.540
That’s exactly what we need people like
you to talk about."

00:04:31.540 --> 00:04:32.540
Thanks for watching!

